    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d479">

                <pb facs="0633" n="534" xml:id="pg534"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/3293: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-09-28T10:00:00+01:00">September 28, 1936—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 29—11:33 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>363. I learn from an authoritative source that the Spanish delegation has
                    submitted to the Secretary General documentary evidence of violations of the
                    non-intervention agreement by Germany, Italy and Portugal. So far this evidence
                    has not been made public<anchor n="76" xml:id="d479-f1"/> and it is not yet
                    clear what developments may result from its submission to the Secretariat.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d479-f1" n="76" xml:id="d479-f1-content">
                <p>Printed by the Spanish Government and circulated, on September 30, 1936, to all
                    the delegations at Geneva and to the press. Copies of Spanish White Paper. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">La “non intervention” dans les Affaires d’Espagne:
                        Documents public’s par le Gouvernement de la République Espagnole</hi>,
                    transmitted to the Department with despatch No. X–27, November 8, 1936, from the
                    Embassy in Madrid, not printed. (852.00/3914)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
